{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle","id":1391903,"title":"[Technocracy Reloaded] So I'm doing a Technocracy Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-27T05:39:23-07:00","id":1391903,"title":"[Technocracy Reloaded] So I'm doing a Technocracy Chronicle","content":"My V5 players have gotten done playing THE FALL OF LONDON and are anxious to get into LET THE STREETS RUN RED but they're also dedicated Mage guys, so they were all following the Technocracy Reloaded Kickstarter. I, ironically, was the last one because I've always favored a antagonist Technocracy and was put off by the Revised Convention books [with the exception of the NWO--that opening and closing fiction was dope].<br /> <br /> So, I backed the Kickstarter and really enjoyed the manuscript. My players thus asked me to do a Chronicle about it and based on the material inside. I thought people might be interested in what I used the book for and how it's going so far.<br /> <br /> 1. The game takes place in 2020 and is post <b>Avatar Storm</b>. A good two-thirds of the Technocratic Union was killed during the chaos of that event and they haven't entirely rebuilt themselves or their influence in the subsequent two decades despite cancelling the <b>Pogrom</b>. The <b>Traditions</b> and Technocracy generally try to do their best to ignore each other's existence with varying degrees of success.<br /> <br /> 2. The player characters are based out of a gated community called <b>Happydale, WV</b> which is a suburbia that's been <b>terranormed</b> by the Union. All of the children are educated in super-science, its jobs are all related to marketing computers, and it's eeriely propsperous in all respects with some underground labs. The first couple of sessions are just to give players a sense of what a Technocratic Utopia is about for better and worse.<br /> <br /> 3. The player characters' mission is going to be related to a town called <b>Saint Claire</b> appearing in Pennsylvania after collectively disappearing for 16 years. No one is noticing due to a heavy Arcane factor [I forget what the Union called that background] but it's a former town owned and operated by the <b>Special Projects Division</b> and had a Construct with over two dozen Enlightened Scientists working inside it. If everyone is sane and uncorrupted, then it would be a massive boost for the Union.<br /> <br /> 4. Complicating the issue is that a child-murderer/kidnapper called <b>The Nappy Napper</b> (a Ronin Bone Gnawer) has taken some children in the area that's drawn national media attention. The Union is confused because, werewolf or not, the local construct should have been able to handle this as well as keep it out of the media just as the Union was about to reintegrate the area (or sanitize it).<br /> <br /> 5. It'll be an adaptation of &quot;The Saint Claire Contract&quot; from <b>Project: Twilight</b> which was a mission for the FBI Special Affairs Division. In this case, the PCs going in as SAD FBI impersonators in order to investigate the area and &quot;solve&quot; the case. Part of the fun will be their superiors clearly not giving a shit about a local serial killer vs. shutting down Unelightened reporters and true crime enthusiasts poking into their business.<br /> <br /> 6. The twist of the Chronicle, which isn't much of a twist, is that the head of the SPD Construct is a corrupted <b>Syndicate</b> infernalist who was corrupted by working with Pentex years ago. The actual twist is <b>Michael Norge</b> is NOT a Nephandi. He genuinely believes using Dimensional Science and making pacts with hostile aliens is in the Union's best interests. I'll have him make an argument that the PCs should accept expansive bribes and let him negotiate with Pentex to restore the Union's former financial basis.<br /> <br /> 7. There's non-corrupted Special Affairs Division, Progenitor, and NWO people in the town who all have their own agendas as well as reflect a Technocracy that no longer exists. The fact that the Union is now at (semi) peace with the Traditions, that its now weakened, and (jokingly) WHO is President will be fun to handle.<br /> <br /> 8. I'll have fun with the fact that the <b>Siren Cosmetics Construct</b> has a lot of cloning facilities and what terrible personal horror can be used from them. Michael Norge will attempt to &quot;replace&quot; the children taken by the Nappy Napper and have a local homeless man blamed for the atrocities to get the media away. Also, he's planning on introducing a &quot;new&quot; breed of cloned agent to the Union and mostly thinks this will be his way to buy back into the Union (an <b>Enticer Formori</b> made from a local cheerleader). He doesn't realize in the new Union that clones have rights.<br /> <br /> 9. There's also a small werewolf pack (<b>The Steppenwolves</b>) sniffing around the area since the local Garou know a town appeared out of nowhere and they smell Wyrm taint from the Siren Cosmetics plant. They get easily distracted by the Nappy Napper since he's a disgrace to the Garou race, though. Were they to try to attack the Construct, they'd get slaughtered as they have no idea what they're dealing with.<br /> <br /> 10. The whole point will be the PCs deciding where their priorities lay and what the best way to help the Union is. They can make a deal with Michael Norge and the SPD to get billions flooding back into the Union, they can try to remove the corruption, they can focus on stopping a child-killing reality deviant, or they can just order the entire place sanitized to the ground (difficult but not impossible).<br /> <br /> Any thoughts, ideas?<br /> <br /> Should be a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-27-2020, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T09:41:49-07:00","id":1391974,"title":"","content":"3. Cloaking is the Technocratic equivalent of Arcane.<br /> <br /> Sounds like an interesting chronicle with lots of options. You've also got some structure by remixing prior WoD material. I like the twist with the SPD head, Michael Norge. Not every evil spiritsummoner need be Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T09:54:01-07:00","id":1391978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1391974#post1391974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Cloaking is the Technocratic equivalent of Arcane.<br /> <br /> Sounds like an interesting chronicle with lots of options. You've also got some structure by remixing prior WoD material. I like the twist with the SPD head, Michael Norge. Not every evil spiritsummoner need be Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the goal of the campaign is to let the player characters actually define what sort of Union chronicle they want to pursue. The people of Saint Claire are Unionists Pre-Avatar Storm with lots of brainwashing, hidden corruption, plans for genocide, and absolute power from its heads. The player characters are the new breed of Technocrats who have a lot less power but a lot more operational freedom.<br /> <br /> They could make an alliance with Norge and reinstitute the SPD in the Syndicate which will, yes, having them dealing with demons but maybe they could feel like the Union could TAKE over Pentex and perhaps start rebuilding its global power base. After all, not all of them are Wyrm cultists. Some deal with demons purely for profit.<br /> <br /> They could also focus on the very personal human drama going on of the murders and kidnappings--believing the politica are not their problem and potentially miss the bigger picture.<br /> <br /> Or they may try to act morally against a very immoral set of situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:11:07-07:00","id":1392000,"title":"","content":"Sounds awesome. Wish I could play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T13:57:46-07:00","id":1392041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392000#post1392000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds awesome. Wish I could play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> I think I can stretch it into a campaign until the next V5 Chronicle book but I'm also debating looking into other Mage Chronicles and books to follow up on it.<br /> <br /> Visiting MECHA as a New TechnocratTM might be interesting, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T14:38:34-07:00","id":1392051,"title":"","content":"Cool, sound awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T18:54:32-07:00","id":1392382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392041#post1392041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> I think I can stretch it into a campaign until the next V5 Chronicle book but I'm also debating looking into other Mage Chronicles and books to follow up on it.<br /> <br /> Visiting MECHA as a New TechnocratTM might be interesting, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike VtM, MtAs doesn't seem to have many of those pre-made chronicles, especially when it comes to dedicated chronicle books rather than short ones added to other books and the vast majority of them assumes the PCs are at least Mages if not Traditionalists rather than Technocrats. I know because I'm actually looking around at those adventures right now and thinking about how I restructure them for M20 (with the possibility of use for a Technocrat game). Basically a couple months ago, before everything became one big mess with Covid, I ran a V20 game where I took a bunch of the old Chicago Chronicles for VtM, changed up some things, tossed out some of the wonkier stuff, etc. It was fairly successful and I had been thinking of doing a follow up with some of the later Chicago material but then the virus canned all that.<br /> <br /> So I had set all that aside... until the Technocracy Reloaded kickstarter happened.<br /> <br /> Since I'm in a MtAs mood right now, I thought about looking at the old Mage chronicles and seeing about doing what I had with the Chicago Chronicles. Unfortunately like I said, there doesn't seem to be as many of them for MtAs as there was VtM and all the Rev Ed ones are tied to the metaplot and race to the original end of MtAs, making them ill suited for starting off such a Chronicle. But they could work for your purposes. Though outside of <i>Ascension</i> and it's whole Time of Judgement, most are short things. Manifesto: Transmissions from the Rogue Council has the Alien Avatar chronicle, which haven't gotten to yet and don't fully remember, did involve some things from the Second World War and the Tradition/Technocracy alliance that formed during that time as well as of course the involvement of the Rogue Council which from the Technocracy PoV would be seen as a major threat. So there is some potential there you could mine.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I've been looking at earlier stuff like Chaos Factor and Loom of Fate, the latter of which actually makes more sense if you swap out the main antagonists being Technocrats for Mages/Nephandi, making it more open for a Technocrat game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T18:57:58-07:00","id":1392383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392382#post1392382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment, I've been looking at earlier stuff like Chaos Factor and Loom of Fate, the latter of which actually makes more sense if you swap out the main antagonists being Technocrats for Mages/Nephandi, making it more open for a Technocrat game.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Boromir voice: </span></b><i><span style=\"font-size:14px\">One does not simply swap out Samuel Haight.</span></i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T19:11:18-07:00","id":1392386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392383#post1392383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\