e":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:08:11-07:00","id":1392488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392382#post1392382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment, I've been looking at earlier stuff like Chaos Factor and Loom of Fate, the latter of which actually makes more sense if you swap out the main antagonists being Technocrats for Mages/Nephandi, making it more open for a Technocrat game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loom of Fate also works better if you remove the stuff about previously-unmentioned werewolves carrying out a DEM offscreen. Because if the climax of your narrative is a moral dilemma, removing it of all force doesn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:18:11-07:00","id":1392542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392488#post1392488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Loom of Fate also works better if you remove the stuff about previously-unmentioned werewolves carrying out a DEM offscreen. Because if the climax of your narrative is a moral dilemma, removing it of all force doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I had completely forgotten about that particular potential ending simply because of how insignificant it was.<br /> <br /> Though amusingly one of the things I've been playing with is using Loom as a starting point for Chaos Factor, with Haight being the villain, having found a ritual that will supposedly steal an Avatar and bind it to another, with Norna being his intended victim. Which of course brings in werewolves looking for him. So I could actually have something like that happen and it not be entirely out of nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T11:52:59-07:00","id":1392613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392542#post1392542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I had completely forgotten about that particular potential ending simply because of how insignificant it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes the whole conflict of the module pointless.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turn an innocent girl into a pattern spider or risk death and destruction to the city via earthquake?&quot;<br /> <br /> Only if you choose the latter, members of another splat who the PCs never interact with or <i>even learn exist </i>solve the problem offscreen with 0 downsides.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T21:58:02-07:00","id":1392755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392613#post1392613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes the whole conflict of the module pointless.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turn an innocent girl into a pattern spider or risk death and destruction to the city via earthquake?&quot;<br /> <br /> Only if you choose the latter, members of another splat who the PCs never interact with or <i>even learn exist </i>solve the problem offscreen with 0 downsides.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Technically they didn't actually stop it, they just delayed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:09:53-07:00","id":1393000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle#post1391903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> <br /> 5. It'll be an adaptation of &quot;The Saint Claire Contract&quot; from <b>Project: Twilight</b> which was a mission for the FBI Special Affairs Division. In this case, the PCs going in as SAD FBI impersonators in order to investigate the area and &quot;solve&quot; the case. Part of the fun will be their superiors clearly not giving a shit about a local serial killer vs. shutting down Unelightened reporters and true crime enthusiasts poking into their business...</div> </div> </div> </div>So instead of being SAD agents, they are Technocrats? I like it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T07:08:11-07:00","id":1398770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392755#post1392755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically they didn't actually stop it, they just delayed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>For about 100 years or so IIRC, which functionally solves it for the rest of the chronicle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:41:39-07:00","id":1400648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1392382#post1392382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment, I've been looking at earlier stuff like Chaos Factor and Loom of Fate, the latter of which actually makes more sense if you swap out the main antagonists being Technocrats for Mages/Nephandi, making it more open for a Technocrat game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had an idea for Loom today. <br /> <br /> The original cabal of mages who &quot;solved&quot; the Norna Weaver issue back in the '90s has had a run in with paradox and written themselves out of existence. <br /> <br /> Now that the cabal who &quot;originally&quot; helped Norna to awaken no longer exist, Norna Weaver and the Pattern Spider are in a state of flux. One moment, Norna is the Spider. Another, the web is destroyed and Norna is no longer awakened. The effects of these changes ripple throughout San Francisco, as reality tries to set time right again. Time Mages of both the technocracy and traditions have noticed the ripples leading to Norna or the Pattern Spider, respectively. Now there is an opportunity to use time travel to follow these time ripples back to their source... and now the PC's need to set things right, but which right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:43:53-07:00","id":1400649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1398770#post1398770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For about 100 years or so IIRC, which functionally solves it for the rest of the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a copy of Loom of Fate but I was always a bit frustrated by that; not that I was opposed by the &quot;unexpected nothing&quot; that occurs, but that the explanation was hidden away in some werewolf module and I was never able to find out the details on that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:38:43-07:00","id":1400718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1400648#post1400648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had an idea for Loom today.<br /> <br /> The original cabal of mages who &quot;solved&quot; the Norna Weaver issue back in the '90s has had a run in with paradox and written themselves out of existence.<br /> <br /> Now that the cabal who &quot;originally&quot; helped Norna to awaken no longer exist, Norna Weaver and the Pattern Spider are in a state of flux. One moment, Norna is the Spider. Another, the web is destroyed and Norna is no longer awakened. The effects of these changes ripple throughout San Francisco, as reality tries to set time right again. Time Mages of both the technocracy and traditions have noticed the ripples leading to Norna or the Pattern Spider, respectively. Now there is an opportunity to use time travel to follow these time ripples back to their source... and now the PC's need to set things right, but which right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Biggest issue with using Loom of Fate in any way in the modern setting is that it involves the Technocracy being willing and knowing servants of the Weaver from WTA. It was very early 1e in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T22:00:51-07:00","id":1400903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391903-technocracy-reloaded-so-i-m-doing-a-technocracy-chronicle?p=1400718#post1400718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Biggest issue with using Loom of Fate in any way in the modern setting is that it involves the Technocracy being willing and knowing servants of the Weaver from WTA. It was very early 1e in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall from the module, the Technocracy wasn't a servant of Cob. In fact, I think the text says they <i>created</i> Cob, long ago to stabilize the region. The fact that Cob is a giant spider spirit was just... coincidence, I guess? Maybe they found some weaver spirit and gave it the ol' technocracy-upgrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-07T19:21:27-07:00","id":1401592,"title":"","content":"Actually the book says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To contain the spirits of the Wyld, the Progenitors and Void Seekers (the old name for the Void Engineers) summoned a powerful pattern spider named Cob, reinforcing it with great power. Over the years, the Technomancers have increased Cob\u2019s might with cybernetic enhancements, Weaver spirit essence, and bio-restoratives. </div> </div> </div>Further it's bio in the NPC section describes it as being 'conjured' by the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it doesn't really come across as something created by the Technocracy. It's just another weird relic of the First Edition when they were still setting things out and not really something that they would do in the game as it currently is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png"